# distinct_numbers:
# CSES 1621, Distinct Numbers (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1621), in our
# own words: how many different values a list of integers holds. The input is a
# Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of binary naturals
# (corpora/library/binary/natural) and the answer a binary natural. Part of the
# CSES port's second batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: an element is counted when it equals
# no element before it, so each value is counted once, at its first place; the
# earlier elements are kept in a list, and each element is compared with every
# one of them. The reading takes about n^2 comparisons for n elements; the
# replacement the family asks for is sorting and counting the changes, or a
# hash set, about n log n or n steps.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only, with no top, no choice and no parallel. It β-reduces to V, the canonical
# binary numeral of the answer (each fold consumes a finite list). So ⊢_β P = V,
# and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual
# preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self candidate elements
    . elements false λelement rest. merge_binary_equality element candidate true (self candidate rest)
  )
λ member
. (λtuple. tuple λelements. fixpoint (λself earlier count rest. rest count λelement others. member element earlier (self earlier count others) (self (cons element earlier) (merge_binary_increment count) others)) nil binary_zero elements)
λ distinct_numbers
. export distinct_numbers
